- c670 [design_decision | 7m2jV7BOFkA @ 1923-1931s]
  Instead of using the ollama run command in the terminal each time, interact with the llama model using an API through Python.
- c2306 [design_decision | egFqsJQ9kuY @ 750-764s]
  The custom collate function includes code to move input and target tensors to a specific device (CPU, CUDA, or MPS) during data loading.
- c2307 [fact | egFqsJQ9kuY @ 757-764s]
  The device can be CPU, CUDA for GPUs, or MPS for Macs with Apple silicon chips.
- c2308 [design_decision | egFqsJQ9kuY @ 766-834s]
  Performing device transfer in the custom collate function (outside the training loop) allows the transfer to happen as a background process, preventing it from blocking the GPU during model training.
- c2309 [code | egFqsJQ9kuY @ 839-847s]
  device = torch.device('cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu')
- c2310 [fact | egFqsJQ9kuY @ 869-878s]
  For MacBooks with Apple silicon chips, the device can be set to torch.device('mps') for faster execution.
- c3469 [fact | yXrGeDNuymY @ 259-271s]
  OpenAI originally saved GPT-2 weights using TensorFlow, while the lecture series code uses PyTorch.
- c3470 [design_decision | yXrGeDNuymY @ 271-279s]
  TensorFlow must be installed to load the GPT-2 weights, which were originally saved in TensorFlow format.
- c3471 [design_decision | yXrGeDNuymY @ 271-279s]
  TQDM library is installed to track the download progress of the weights.
- c3472 [hyperparameter | yXrGeDNuymY @ 286-294s]
  TensorFlow version should be greater than or equal to 2.15.
- c3473 [hyperparameter | yXrGeDNuymY @ 286-294s]
  TQDM library version should be greater than or equal to 4.66.
- c3861 [design_decision | zuj_NJNouAA @ 3288-3299s]
  The code can run on CPU, CUDA GPU, or Apple silicon chips, with Apple silicon being approximately 2x faster than Apple CPU.